            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of alpha-1-noracetylmethadol. A facile N-demethylation of alpha-1-acetylmethadol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>630-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A facile N-demethylation of the narcotic analgesic, alpha-1-acetylmethadol, was accomplished by allowing it to react with mercuric acetate under reflux in dilute acetic acid. The product, alpha-1-noracetylmethadol, was isolated as the hydrochloride in 50% yield. Methadone, when allowed to react with mercuric acetate under the same conditions, did not undergo N-demethylation and was recovered unchanged.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
